        "title": "List the arrangements",
        "body": "There are $\\frac{4!}{2!}=12$ different numbers. The first and last digits have an even sum when both are odd ($3$ and $5$) or both are even ($2$ and $2$).\n- Ends $3\\ldots5$ or $5\\ldots3$ with $22$ in the middle: $3225$, $5223$.\n- Ends $2\\ldots2$ with $3,5$ in the middle: $2352$, $2532$.\n\nThat's $4$ of $12$, probability $\\frac13$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac13$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Choose the end positions",
        "body": "Think of the four digit cards $2,2,3,5$ placed at random. The pair of cards in the first and last positions is equally likely to be any of the $\\binom42=6$ pairs of cards. Even sums come from $\\{2,2\\}$ and $\\{3,5\\}$: $2$ of the $6$ pairs, so the probability is $\\frac13$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac13$**"
      }
