    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Triangle minus two sectors",
        "body": "Let $O_1$, $O_2$ be the centres ($O_1O_2=20$) and $T$ the point of tangency on the second circle. Then $\\angle O_1TO_2=90^\\circ$, $O_2T=10$, so $O_1T=\\sqrt{400-100}=10\\sqrt3$, $\\angle TO_1O_2=30^\\circ$ and $\\angle TO_2O_1=60^\\circ$.\n\nThe shaded region is the part of triangle $O_1TO_2$ outside both circles:\n- triangle: $\\frac12\\cdot10\\cdot10\\sqrt3=50\\sqrt3\\approx86.60$,\n- sector of circle 1 with angle $30^\\circ$: $\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot100\\pi\\approx26.18$,\n- sector of circle 2 with angle $60^\\circ$: $\\frac16\\cdot100\\pi\\approx52.36$.\n\nShaded area $\\approx86.60-26.18-52.36=8.06$, i.e. about $8$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 8**"
      }
